fields.evidenceCards/0/content:
47 responses from 240 beta participants. Free-text question 'How would you describe the new dashboard' — 31 responses.

19 comments contain 'confusing' or 'unclear'. When analyzed, they fall into three groups:
— 11 about finding metrics: 'unclear where turnover went', 'can't find write-offs', 'half the numbers are gone';
— 5 about the four key metrics themselves: 'unclear why these specific ones were chosen', 'the large numbers are not the ones I need';
— 3 general: 'beautiful but confusing', 'confusing at first, but fine now'.

12 comments are positive, mostly about speed.

fields.evidenceCards/1/content:
240 beta participants over six weeks:
— the 'More metrics' expander was opened at least once by 78% of users, in 61% of all sessions;
— median time to first action with a metric: 9 seconds on the new dashboard vs. 21 on the old one;
— sessions per user per week: 4.1 vs. 3.6 for the same people before the transition;
— out of the four key metrics, one ('Stock on hand') is interacted with in only 6% of sessions, while the other three range from 34% to 51%;
— 14 out of 240 asked support to roll them back to the old dashboard. All 14 belong to the same segment: chains with multiple locations.

fields.evidenceCards/3/content:
Estimates from the designer and head of development:
— an onboarding tour highlighting the expander: three days, mostly design;
— ability to customize the four key metrics: eight days; addresses the 'why these' complaint, but at the cost of the product losing its default opinion;
— multi-location comparison in the main part of the screen for chains: about three weeks, which is a different layout, not a quick fix.

Chains with multiple locations make up 11% of beta participants and 40% of this section's revenue.

The release can be delayed by two weeks without breaking external commitments. Any further delay hits the peak season.
